{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Elaboration","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Elaboration","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":44,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.IsLeibnizAlgebra.left_leibniz","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.IsLeibnizAlgebra.left_leibniz","kind":"theorem","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L337-L337","doc":"Left Leibniz identity:\n`[U, [V, W]] = [[U, V], W] + [V, [U, W]]` pointwise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.IsLeibnizAlgebra.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.IsLeibnizAlgebra.mk","kind":"ctor","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L333-L333","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.IsLeibnizAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.IsLeibnizAlgebra","kind":"structure","line":327,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L327-L339","doc":"Marker structure: a Leibniz algebra is a module with a bilinear bracket\nsatisfying the left Leibniz identity.  We record this as a `Prop`-valued\nstructure witnessing that the q-bracket on horizontal fields forms a\nLeibniz algebra.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:q-jacobiator}`, conclusion at line 571. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.jacobi_identity_violation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.jacobi_identity_violation","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L274-L305","doc":"When `dθ|_{H×H}` is non-degenerate and `q ≠ 1`, the Jacobiator is\ngenerically non-zero.  This witnesses that `(𝔛(M), [·,·]_q)` violates\nthe Jacobi identity for all `q ≠ 1`.\n\nMore precisely: given a point where the cyclic sum\n`Σ_cyc dθ(V,W) L_ξ U ≠ 0` (which is generically true by non-degeneracy\nof the Levi form), the Jacobiator is non-zero.\n\nLaTeX: Proposition in `qou-elaboration.tex`, lines 551–572. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.q_jacobiator_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.q_jacobiator_classical","kind":"theorem","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L265-L272","doc":"The Jacobiator vanishes at `q = 1` (classical Jacobi identity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.q_jacobiator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.q_jacobiator","kind":"def","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L251-L263","doc":"The Jacobiator of the q-deformed Lie bracket applied to three horizontal\nvector fields.  For horizontal `U, V, W` (i.e. `θ(U) = θ(V) = θ(W) = 0`),\nthe bracket reduces to `[V,W]_q = q⁻¹[V,W]`, and the Jacobiator is\n`Jac_q(U,V,W) = −q⁻¹(1−q⁻¹) Σ_cyc dθ(V,W) L_ξ U`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{prop:q-jacobiator}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.dq_squared_nonvanishing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.dq_squared_nonvanishing","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L209-L247","doc":"`d_q²` does not vanish in general (unlike the classical `d² = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.dq_squared_nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.dq_squared_nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L194-L207","doc":"When `q ≠ 1` and `dθ ∧ L_ξ α ≠ 0`, `d_q² α ≠ 0`.\nThis is the precise statement that the Jacobi identity fails. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.dq_squared_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.dq_squared_classical","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L187-L192","doc":"At `q = 1`, `d_q² = 0` (recovers the classical `d² = 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.dq_squared_explicit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.dq_squared_explicit","kind":"def","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L180-L185","doc":"The explicit `d_q²` obstruction: `d_q²(α) = q⁻¹(1 − q⁻¹) · (dθ ∧ L_ξ α)`.\n\nHere `dtheta_Lxi_alpha` represents `dθ ∧ L_ξ α` at each point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.BringsSurfaceCircleBundle.branch_points","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.BringsSurfaceCircleBundle.branch_points","kind":"def","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L153-L153","doc":"Number of branch points (= 6, matching χ = −6). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.BringsSurfaceCircleBundle.covering_degree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.BringsSurfaceCircleBundle.covering_degree","kind":"def","line":151,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L151-L151","doc":"The degree of the branched covering `S → CP¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.BringsSurfaceCircleBundle.genus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.BringsSurfaceCircleBundle.genus","kind":"def","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L149-L149","doc":"The genus of the base. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.BringsSurfaceCircleBundle.M","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.BringsSurfaceCircleBundle.M","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L147-L147","doc":"The circle bundle `M_S`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.BringsSurfaceCircleBundle.base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.BringsSurfaceCircleBundle.base","kind":"def","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L145-L145","doc":"The base Riemann surface (genus 4). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.BringsSurfaceCircleBundle.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.BringsSurfaceCircleBundle.mk","kind":"ctor","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L143-L143","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.BringsSurfaceCircleBundle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.BringsSurfaceCircleBundle","kind":"structure","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L136-L153","doc":"**Bring's surface circle bundle**: the unit circle bundle\n`M_S ⊂ T*S` where `S` is Bring's surface (genus 4).  The Liouville\n1-form restricts to a contact form making `M_S` a 3-dimensional\nstrictly pseudoconvex CR manifold.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{ex:brings-surface}` (in elaboration chapter) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.ALELink.M","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.ALELink.M","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L134-L134","doc":"The link `M = S³/Γ` as a type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.ALELink.order_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.ALELink.order_pos","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L132-L132","doc":"The order is at least 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.ALELink.group_order","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.ALELink.group_order","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L130-L130","doc":"The finite subgroup order |Γ|. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.ALELink.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.ALELink.mk","kind":"ctor","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L128-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.ALELink","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.ALELink","kind":"structure","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L123-L134","doc":"**ALE link example**: `M = S³/Γ` for a finite subgroup `Γ ⊂ SU(2)`.\nA compact 3-dimensional strictly pseudoconvex CR manifold whose\nReeb field generates the Hopf fibration `S³/Γ → S²`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{ex:ale}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.CalabiYauHypersurface.eulerChar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.CalabiYauHypersurface.eulerChar","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L121-L121","doc":"Euler characteristic of the hypersurface (K3 surface: χ = 24). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.CalabiYauHypersurface.cr_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.CalabiYauHypersurface.cr_dim","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L119-L119","doc":"CR dimension is 1 (real dimension 3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.CalabiYauHypersurface.M","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.CalabiYauHypersurface.M","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L117-L117","doc":"The CR hypersurface carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.CalabiYauHypersurface.ambient","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.CalabiYauHypersurface.ambient","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L115-L115","doc":"The ambient Calabi–Yau carrier type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.CalabiYauHypersurface.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.CalabiYauHypersurface.mk","kind":"ctor","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L113-L113","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.CalabiYauHypersurface","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.CalabiYauHypersurface","kind":"structure","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L107-L121","doc":"**Calabi–Yau hypersurface example**: a smooth strictly convex real\nhypersurface `M ⊂ X` in a Calabi–Yau 2-fold (K3 surface) with\nholonomy `SU(2)`, yielding a natural QOU structure.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{ex:calabi-yau}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.GeneralisedLeviConditions.qou_vanishing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.GeneralisedLeviConditions.qou_vanishing","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L103-L103","doc":"QOU vanishing: adjoint and state sections vanish.  Modelled as\nthe existence of a CQuantumObservableUniverse structure on `M`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.GeneralisedLeviConditions.substrate_nondeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.GeneralisedLeviConditions.substrate_nondeg","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L99-L99","doc":"Non-degeneracy of the substrate: `q > 1` is attainable. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.GeneralisedLeviConditions.kohn_rossi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.GeneralisedLeviConditions.kohn_rossi","kind":"def","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L97-L97","doc":"Kohn–Rossi finite-dimensionality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.GeneralisedLeviConditions.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.GeneralisedLeviConditions.mk","kind":"ctor","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L95-L95","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.GeneralisedLeviConditions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.GeneralisedLeviConditions","kind":"structure","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L90-L103","doc":"**Generalised Levi non-degeneracy conditions**: the three conditions\nunder which the QOU framework extends to CR manifolds of arbitrary\nLevi signature `(r, s)`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{rem:levi-generalisation}`, conditions (1)–(3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.KohnRossiFiniteDim.finite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.KohnRossiFiniteDim.finite","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L88-L88","doc":"Each cohomology group is finite (has a `Fintype` instance). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.KohnRossiFiniteDim.cohomology","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.KohnRossiFiniteDim.cohomology","kind":"def","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L86-L86","doc":"The tangential CR cohomology groups (abstract). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.KohnRossiFiniteDim.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.KohnRossiFiniteDim.mk","kind":"ctor","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.KohnRossiFiniteDim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.KohnRossiFiniteDim","kind":"structure","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L77-L88","doc":"**Kohn–Rossi finite-dimensionality**: the tangential CR complex\n`(Ω^{0,•}_b(M), ∂̄_b)` has finite-dimensional cohomology.\n\nThis replaces strict pseudoconvexity for analytic control over\nq-harmonic forms.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{rem:levi-generalisation}`, condition (1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.TQFTDatum.comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.TQFTDatum.comm","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L59-L59","doc":"Commutativity of the Frobenius algebra. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.TQFTDatum.frobeniusForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.TQFTDatum.frobeniusForm","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L57-L57","doc":"Frobenius form `λ : A → k` (cap cobordism). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.TQFTDatum.unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.TQFTDatum.unit","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L55-L55","doc":"Unit `η : k → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.TQFTDatum.mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.TQFTDatum.mul","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L53-L53","doc":"Multiplication `μ : A ⊗ A → A` (pair-of-pants). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.TQFTDatum.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.TQFTDatum.carrier","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The Frobenius algebra carrier. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.TQFTDatum.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.TQFTDatum.mk","kind":"ctor","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Elaboration.TQFTDatum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Elaboration.TQFTDatum","kind":"structure","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Elaboration.lean#L42-L59","doc":"**2d TQFT datum**: a commutative Frobenius algebra `A` over `k`\ntogether with cobordism data.  The product `μ` corresponds to\na pair-of-pants cobordism, the Frobenius form `λ` to a cap.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{rem:tqft-context}` ","signatureChunk":0}]}